---
import Docs from '../../layouts/Docs.astro';
import Example from '../../components/Example.astro';
import Guides from '../../components/Guides.astro';
import sprite from '../../../ds/icons/icons.svg?raw';
import { i } from '../../lib/icon';

const names = [...sprite.matchAll(/id="dd-i-([\w-]+)"/g)].map((m) => m[1]);
const usage = `
<div class="dd-row" style="--dd-gap: var(--dd-space-4); font-size: 22px">
  ${i('home')} ${i('chart')} ${i('database')} ${i('bell')} ${i('sparkle')}
  <span style="color: var(--dd-primary)">${i('heart')}</span>
  <span style="color: var(--dd-ok)">${i('success')}</span>
  <span style="color: var(--dd-bad)">${i('alert')}</span>
</div>`;
const code = `<!-- once per page: the sprite (release/icons.svg), inline or fetched -->
<svg class="dd-icon" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#dd-i-bell"/></svg>
<svg class="dd-icon" role="img" aria-label="Alerts"><use href="#dd-i-bell"/></svg>`;
---
<Docs title="Icons" group="Foundations" lead="Solar by 480 Design, Bold Duotone weight: soft, rounded and two-toned. Small UI glyphs (chevrons, check, close, plus) are thin line strokes so they stay crisp, and the ai family is drawn in the same two-tone style.">
  <h2 id="usage">Usage</h2>
  <p>Icons ship as an SVG sprite (<code>release/icons.svg</code>). Inline it once near the top of <code>&lt;body&gt;</code>, then reference symbols with <code>&lt;use&gt;</code>. Icons inherit <code>currentColor</code> and size to <code>1.15em</code> via <code>.dd-icon</code>.</p>
  <Example code={usage} description="Duotone icons take their colour from the text; the second tone is the same colour at lower opacity." />
  <pre class="dd-mono" style="background: var(--dd-surface); padding: 16px 20px; border-radius: var(--dd-r-box); font-size: 13px; overflow:auto">{code}</pre>
  <p>Need more? Browse the full Solar set on <a href="https://icon-sets.iconify.design/solar/">Iconify</a>, add the names to <code>scripts/fetch-icons.mjs</code> and run it to rebuild the sprite.</p>

  <h2 id="set">The set</h2>
  <p>Click an icon to copy its <code>&lt;use&gt;</code> snippet.</p>
  <div class="doc-icons">
    {names.map((n) => (
      <button class="doc-icon" type="button" data-dd-copy={`<svg class="dd-icon" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#dd-i-${n}"/></svg>`}>
        <Fragment set:html={i(n)} /><span>{n}</span>
      </button>
    ))}
  </div>

  <h2 id="guidelines">Guidelines</h2>
  <Guides do={['Lead labels with icons in buttons and menus.', 'Give icon-only controls an <code>aria-label</code>.', 'Colour icons with status tokens when they carry meaning.']} dont={['Don’t mix in other icon sets.', 'Don’t scale icons past 2× text size inside UI.']} />
</Docs>
